            "input": "rulebook:us_faa_part107"
          },
          "status": "outside",
          "text": "Anti-collision lighting at night and in civil twilight. At night, the remote pilot in command has completed an initial knowledge test or training under 107.65 after April 6, 2021, and the aircraft shows lighted anti-collision lighting visible for at least 3 statute miles. The same lighting is required during civil twilight."
